  "why": "A lighthouse on its own coast at night: a rock cliff over the sea (terrain cliff and coast, a waterBody sea with waves), a tall striped tower on the cliff top. The fire, the glass room, the Fresnel lens and its beams, the grinding lens and its mercury bath all play close on the lantern; the how line pulls back to the beams sweeping over the waves, and the end shows the whole coast with stairs and rocks.",
