     "claim": "Augustin Fresnel invented his lighthouse lens in 1822.",
     "role": "fix2",
     "search": "Augustin Fresnel lens lighthouse 1822"
    },
    {
     "claim": "The beam of a large (first-order) Fresnel lens could be seen about 20 miles out to sea.",
     "role": "how",
     "search": "first order Fresnel lens visible 20 miles"
    },
    {
     "claim": "Big rotating lighthouse lenses floated on a bath of liquid mercury so they turned with very little friction.",
     "role": "fix3",
     "search": "lighthouse lens mercury bath float rotate friction"
    }
   ]
  },
  "sentences": [
   {
    "role": "hook",
    "text": "If you light a fire on a tall tower, you have a lighthouse."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem",
    "text": "But the wind on top blows the flame out."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix1",
    "text": "So you close the flame inside a glass room."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem2",
    "text": "But now its glow is weak and spreads every way."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix2",
    "text": "So you add a lens, invented in 1822, that bends the glow into beams."
   },
   {
    "role": "name",
    "text": "This is a Fresnel lens."
   },
   {
    "role": "how",
    "text": "The lens turns, and its beam is seen about 20 miles out to sea."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem3",
    "text": "But now the heavy lens grinds as it turns."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix3",
    "text": "So you float it on liquid mercury, and it spins easily."
   },
   {
    "role": "finish",
    "text": "Add stairs to the door and rocks around the base."
   },
   {
    "role": "congrats",
    "text": "Congratulations, you have built a lighthouse."
   }
  ],
